ug 2080097 - Release UDPSocketParent on its owning thread after Connect.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339536\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342090\n", "files": ["dom/network/UDPSocketParent.cpp"], "git_node": "3902506cdb6bd649c027b3aff3aea84e76cecce4", "git_parents": ["e9f2a326147107940ca80d48023520b610f031bb"], "node": "18398f1f68efed5fe132182498ef3024f019be7c", "parents": ["733cb79a90c77fcca0e536002de7634d68962890"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584358, "git_changesets": ["3902506cdb6bd649c027b3aff3aea84e76cecce4"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1269": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084816 - patch for esr153  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342454\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.cpp", "gfx/layers/client/TextureClient.h"], "git_node": "5e7db6b432c83a34dd807da56e35e61eea4d5063", "git_parents": ["3902506cdb6bd649c027b3aff3aea84e76cecce4"], "node": "8fe6dff47ef08ee7c247316d5cb0703185ca8724", "parents": ["18398f1f68efed5fe132182498ef3024f019be7c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584381, "git_changesets": ["5e7db6b432c83a34dd807da56e35e61eea4d5063"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1270": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088854.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341614\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341919\n", "files": ["gfx/skia/skia/src/core/SkAnalyticEdge.h", "gfx/skia/skia/src/core/SkEdgeBuilder.cpp", "gfx/skia/skia/src/core/SkEdgeBuilder.h", "gfx/skia/skia/src/core/SkScan_AAAPath.cpp"], "git_node": "984f82bf3a8c0ac84e8442e11f0ffa110206882e", "git_parents": ["5e7db6b432c83a34dd807da56e35e61eea4d5063"], "node": "8471f6dbeb7eeda81f10d49350e61f9494d062ba", "parents": ["8fe6dff47ef08ee7c247316d5cb0703185ca8724"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584406, "git_changesets": ["984f82bf3a8c0ac84e8442e11f0ffa110206882e"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1271": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1860128 - Don't panic when adding a font fails.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340270\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342456\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wr_glyph_rasterizer/src/platform/unix/font.rs"], "git_node": "0498fc66ce48bfbd02ba0778391cff48099d790c", "git_parents": ["984f82bf3a8c0ac84e8442e11f0ffa110206882e"], "node": "1ec36dd879f8274a750840dd5e01c757ff0083ae", "parents": ["8471f6dbeb7eeda81f10d49350e61f9494d062ba"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584430, "git_changesets": ["0498fc66ce48bfbd02ba0778391cff48099d790c"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1272": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073689 - Register VideoBridgeParent after taking a reference to it.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335662\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340013\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/VideoBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/VideoBridgeParent.h"], "git_node": "77c61e6d72cfda44625f34fb0320181acfb89428", "git_parents": ["0498fc66ce48bfbd02ba0778391cff48099d790c"], "node": "68a130ef6b4a54e0da97af6256cb9376727df2c2", "parents": ["1ec36dd879f8274a750840dd5e01c757ff0083ae"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584459, "git_changesets": ["77c61e6d72cfda44625f34fb0320181acfb89428"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1273": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091445.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341440\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341779\n", "files": ["third_party/rust/icu_collator_data/data/collation_root_v1.rs.data", "third_party/rust/icu_collator_data/data/collation_tailoring_v1.rs.data"], "git_node": "f77f0602892ddc6ae814449121828ad721355f1d", "git_parents": ["77c61e6d72cfda44625f34fb0320181acfb89428"], "node": "37f4931101912edb58eb53f517b18bee72af3d0e", "parents": ["68a130ef6b4a54e0da97af6256cb9376727df2c2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584487, "git_changesets": ["f77f0602892ddc6ae814449121828ad721355f1d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1274": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Report a slice as cloneable only when its wrapped stream is  a=pascalc\n\nSlicedInputStream::GetCloneable() returned true whenever the wrapped stream\nimplemented nsICloneableInputStream, but implementing that interface does not\nmean a stream can be cloned right now: nsMultiplexInputStream and\nnsBufferedInputStream both refuse once they have been read from.  Callers that\ncheck before cloning, such as NS_InputStreamIsCloneable(), were told yes and\nthen got a failure out of Clone().  Delegate to the wrapped stream, the way\nnsBufferedInputStream already does.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328176\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341874\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/SlicedInputStream.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestSlicedInputStream.cpp"], "git_node": "a3cc02532eaf98d0266e3dde5fc2563e1592e932", "git_parents": ["f77f0602892ddc6ae814449121828ad721355f1d"], "node": "d49d8eedaf2fb120ee719be5076d442b5f4e979d", "parents": ["37f4931101912edb58eb53f517b18bee72af3d0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Reject an upload stream that NormalizeUploadStream can't make cloneable  a=pascalc\n\nNormalizeUploadStream() promises that a parent-process upload stream is\ncloneable, seekable and synchronous, but the nsIBufferedInputStream and\nnsIMultiplexInputStream branches normalized the streams they wrap and then\nreturned the wrapper untouched, even when the wrapper itself could not be\ncloned because it had already been read from.  Callers that rely on the\nguarantee, such as HttpBaseChannel::CloneUploadStream and\nnsHttpTransaction::Init, are then left unable to clone it.\n\nCheck whether the stream can be used as-is first, and fail when a wrapper\nwould otherwise be returned unchanged, as that means it has been read from\nand can't be rebuilt without losing the data it has buffered.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328177\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341875\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_upload_stream_normalization.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "1a807bf47743c9ee96538b65262d643b8c0ee650", "git_parents": ["a3cc02532eaf98d0266e3dde5fc2563e1592e932"], "node": "4474bfff4fd9611e4b41ac19cfd0054eecc01d45", "parents": ["d49d8eedaf2fb120ee719be5076d442b5f4e979d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Clear nsMultiplexInputStream's read state when seeking back to the start.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341822\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341876\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/nsMultiplexInputStream.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestMultiplexInputStream.cpp"], "git_node": "f953aec719e99a5cbb2e5f643788f640ea1febae", "git_parents": ["1a807bf47743c9ee96538b65262d643b8c0ee650"], "node": "1f767c763c8f1c492231e6c5b73dfa332b945773", "parents": ["4474bfff4fd9611e4b41ac19cfd0054eecc01d45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Don't fall back to sharing a seekable upload stream with the socket thread  a=pascalc\n\nnsHttpTransaction::Init() reads the channel's own upload stream when it cannot\nclone it, which leaves the socket thread reading a stream the main thread may\nrewind for a redirect or an auth retry.  InternalSetUploadStream now refuses an\nupload stream that can't be cloned, so in the parent process make the fallback\nan error for seekable streams rather than sharing them, and assert that it\nisn't reached.  A stream the channel cannot rewind, such as an async pipe, is\nstill read directly.\n\nThe socket process is exempt: it reads its own deserialized copy of the body,\nwhich nothing else touches and which may not be cloneable (a file stream sent\nas a descriptor never is outside the parent).\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328178\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341877\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp"], "git_node": "cb4f9c261ae25184687440cdc79924503aafe27a", "git_parents": ["f953aec719e99a5cbb2e5f643788f640ea1febae"], "node": "07a714c28b7c887acabb6abba5d0b26b9ebf476b", "parents": ["1f767c763c8f1c492231e6c5b73dfa332b945773"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794584529, "git_changesets": ["a3cc02532eaf98d0266e3dde5fc2563e1592e932", "1a807bf47743c9ee96538b65262d643b8c0ee650", "f953aec719e99a5cbb2e5f643788f640ea1febae", "cb4f9c261ae25184687440cdc79924503aafe27a"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1275": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090172: Hold a strong reference to the main-thread XHR across worker abort.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340567\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342185\n", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.cpp"], "git_node": "3b108b43523edcaa0546198aa36cb8e42ce826bc", "git_parents": ["cb4f9c261ae25184687440cdc79924503aafe27a"], "node": "fbf7b3d45332cd895172a75c6f7e14fe6aa96a5d", "parents": ["07a714c28b7c887acabb6abba5d0b26b9ebf476b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794590927, "git_changesets": ["3b108b43523edcaa0546198aa36cb8e42ce826bc"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1276": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1973071 - Expand AddonManager.getInstallForURL's add-on validation  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nAdd optional `id` and `type` options to `AddonManager.getInstallForURL()`, so\nthat the caller can specify the expected add-on type and ID. When provided,\nthose details should be checked against the provided add-on before it is\ninstalled.\n\nAlso expand enforcement of the existing `version` option for fresh installs and\nmanual upgrades. Previously, that was only checked when the existing add-on was\nalready known (e.g. updates via `addon.findUpdates()`).\n\nFix some related tests, one of which passed a mismatched version, and some\nothers that failed to pass through the add-on name + version due to a typo.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326452\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342700\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_install.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_install_expected_addon_details.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "333a3ee98fa42dc7e8e3e11c0a3988315ee7cfbe", "git_parents": ["3b108b43523edcaa0546198aa36cb8e42ce826bc"], "node": "0e18d09de2776e02812b77752958c2af02e42a0d", "parents": ["fbf7b3d45332cd895172a75c6f7e14fe6aa96a5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076009 - Pass expected add-on details when installing recommended+builtin add-ons  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333214\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342701\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabResourceMapping.sys.mjs", "devtools/client/shared/remote-debugging/adb/adb-addon.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/recommended-addon-card.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_warning_messages.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_installssl.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_signed_verify.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_system_upgrades.js"], "git_node": "83b32711589c0e7649b2fa8497199873dfcb408e", "git_parents": ["333a3ee98fa42dc7e8e3e11c0a3988315ee7cfbe"], "node": "e722dd4e8f8e779c5cd6eb1de18b6d34eaf35dc1", "parents": ["0e18d09de2776e02812b77752958c2af02e42a0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076009 - Pass expected add-on details when installing locales+dictionaries  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333215\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342702\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/dialogs/browserLanguages.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/languages/browser_browser_languages_subdialog.js", "intl/locale/LangPackMatcher.sys.mjs", "intl/locale/tests/unit/test_langPackMatcher_install.js", "intl/locale/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/AddonRepository.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_AddonRepository_langpacks.js"], "git_node": "0ffd72a77fa6d3304ea431660b05c5c3a843cc74", "git_parents": ["83b32711589c0e7649b2fa8497199873dfcb408e"], "node": "2511badf48cddbd079f199f53cde97692130db1f", "parents": ["e722dd4e8f8e779c5cd6eb1de18b6d34eaf35dc1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076009 - Pass expected add-on details when installing themes  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333216\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342703\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-management.js"], "git_node": "7c389df303da0100e7956bc1805b6661416aac76", "git_parents": ["0ffd72a77fa6d3304ea431660b05c5c3a843cc74"], "node": "2498588938a453b6716eee6c896d7c4f517c1329", "parents": ["2511badf48cddbd079f199f53cde97692130db1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076009 - Pass expected add-on details when importing/syncing add-ons  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333217\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342704\n", "files": ["services/sync/modules/addonutils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_AMBrowserExtensionsImport.js"], "git_node": "74d40181c8c536f8b717e813e5df7198d2d7554e", "git_parents": ["7c389df303da0100e7956bc1805b6661416aac76"], "node": "48346cc120f303623fa756d578e4b9d2e081c622", "parents": ["2498588938a453b6716eee6c896d7c4f517c1329"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794592997, "git_changesets": ["333a3ee98fa42dc7e8e3e11c0a3988315ee7cfbe", "83b32711589c0e7649b2fa8497199873dfcb408e", "0ffd72a77fa6d3304ea431660b05c5c3a843cc74", "7c389df303da0100e7956bc1805b6661416aac76", "74d40181c8c536f8b717e813e5df7198d2d7554e"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1277": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068399 - Add some font-list thread-safety annotations.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328457\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342635\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.h"], "git_node": "f91039e2ea759a4fa46d00bd9435520d8ac3e412", "git_parents": ["74d40181c8c536f8b717e813e5df7198d2d7554e"], "node": "49e78adc2b37b3d67cc7447e708349760c28aa2a", "parents": ["48346cc120f303623fa756d578e4b9d2e081c622"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794593025, "git_changesets": ["f91039e2ea759a4fa46d00bd9435520d8ac3e412"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1278": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059024 - Upgrade the consumer count assertion in SharedSurfacesParent::AddTrackingLocked to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340037\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/SharedSurfacesParent.cpp"], "git_node": "2e1e3317dbc3b80868279bbd6ad58c3c5b5c0dbd", "git_parents": ["f91039e2ea759a4fa46d00bd9435520d8ac3e412"], "node": "edbaf6c72fe87789a6d5eeb6d3fdb648ff10cf7d", "parents": ["49e78adc2b37b3d67cc7447e708349760c28aa2a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794593128, "git_changesets": ["2e1e3317dbc3b80868279bbd6ad58c3c5b5c0dbd"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1279": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092632 - disable two NTLM tests which fail after Windows update. DONTBUILD\n\nThe November 2026 update for Windows 11 contained KB 5135557 which caused the\ntest failures. Temporarily disable them until they are fixed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342756\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "7a746bcf867b5b7ef479fd31569b30dcd54c6169", "git_parents": ["2e1e3317dbc3b80868279bbd6ad58c3c5b5c0dbd"], "node": "472132a4ebf64a7afaa0816052351e5189dece66", "parents": ["edbaf6c72fe87789a6d5eeb6d3fdb648ff10cf7d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794602681, "git_changesets": ["7a746bcf867b5b7ef479fd31569b30dcd54c6169"], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "1280": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086816 - enforce some ETSI cryptography minimums for QWACs  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341628\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342326\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/QWACTrustDomain.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/qwac_trust_anchors/test_trust_anchors/test-ca-small-rsa.pem", "security/manager/ssl/qwac_trust_anchors/test_trust_anchors/test-ca-small-rsa.pem.certspec", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-sha1.pem", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-sha1.pem.certspec", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-small-rsa-key.pem", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-small-rsa-key.pem.certspec", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-small-rsa-signature.pem", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs/1-qwac-small-rsa-signature.pem.certspec", "security/manager/ssl/trust-anchor-build-util/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "791703fdc04374fd6b0c6fb774f634780eb3379b", "git_parents": ["7a746bcf867b5b7ef479fd31569b30dcd54c6169"], "node": "abf80694379e2a2b91c38f4f617035fe5e58ff66", "parents": ["472132a4ebf64a7afaa0816052351e5189dece66"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666191, "git_changesets": ["791703fdc04374fd6b0c6fb774f634780eb3379b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1281": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089774 - Use a non-movable load for UnsafeGetReservedSlot.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nThis adds `LoadReservedFixedSlotResult` and uses it instead of `LoadFixedSlotResult`\nfor the `UnsafeGetReservedSlot` intrinsic.\n\nAlso renames `LoadFixedSlotTypedResult` to `LoadReservedFixedSlotTypedResult`\nfor consistency.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341262\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342547\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/IonCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp", "js/src/vm/PortableBaselineInterpret.cpp"], "git_node": "595d751fe3bedb0913e813412f10ef4edd7045bc", "git_parents": ["791703fdc04374fd6b0c6fb774f634780eb3379b"], "node": "a0d6fd04b3eba2d535d8c3419174784280b8cef0", "parents": ["abf80694379e2a2b91c38f4f617035fe5e58ff66"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666288, "git_changesets": ["595d751fe3bedb0913e813412f10ef4edd7045bc"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1282": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091136 - Always merge OSR block parameters with entry block parameters in BacktrackingAllocator.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341297\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342550\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BacktrackingAllocator.cpp", "js/src/jit/BacktrackingAllocator.h"], "git_node": "3773630dff4b047b0afe412ca1d1e25c00ce111d", "git_parents": ["595d751fe3bedb0913e813412f10ef4edd7045bc"], "node": "0efa9454b2cefd8d449ec47bae90cbf53e347ea9", "parents": ["a0d6fd04b3eba2d535d8c3419174784280b8cef0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666331, "git_changesets": ["3773630dff4b047b0afe412ca1d1e25c00ce111d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1283": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078279 - Adjust file stream handling.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336874\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342582\n", "files": ["dom/file/FileBlobImpl.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsFileStreams.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIFileStreams.idl"], "git_node": "852c18811af35be12825f54b950d95589165f9b5", "git_parents": ["3773630dff4b047b0afe412ca1d1e25c00ce111d"], "node": "dad6fc4fec8a634bb9515c8ee585e186bb620ae8", "parents": ["0efa9454b2cefd8d449ec47bae90cbf53e347ea9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666375, "git_changesets": ["852c18811af35be12825f54b950d95589165f9b5"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1284": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089819 - Use a worst-case bound and fallible allocation when calling getIntercepts.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nIn principle this should be more performant, as it means we only make one call\nto getIntercepts, which is where most work happens. The array allocation will\ninitially be oversized, and subsequently truncated to fit the actual number of\nreturned intercepts, but by using fallible allocation we ensure that in an OOM\nsituation it will degrade gracefully (we just bail out of skip-ink processing)\nrather than crashing.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340905\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342628\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp"], "git_node": "57a1410a55fdceee34c6d650e8206543b38dbb24", "git_parents": ["852c18811af35be12825f54b950d95589165f9b5"], "node": "49a2af9a5bbe4022d2b06de3c1ed620284edf406", "parents": ["dad6fc4fec8a634bb9515c8ee585e186bb620ae8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666410, "git_changesets": ["57a1410a55fdceee34c6d650e8206543b38dbb24"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1285": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjfkthame@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090182 - Check for first-letter frame in overflow list.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342170\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342624\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp"], "git_node": "77ccd366e2143aad7346f25d1ebe76d5fa0dd13d", "git_parents": ["57a1410a55fdceee34c6d650e8206543b38dbb24"], "node": "e45adcf4a48b167dab5fdc4a0064fbfa2ca33f44", "parents": ["49a2af9a5bbe4022d2b06de3c1ed620284edf406"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666532, "git_changesets": ["77ccd366e2143aad7346f25d1ebe76d5fa0dd13d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1286": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089592 - Deal with replicated frames in CharacterDataChanged.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341301\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341477\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.h"], "git_node": "f813d9152a23e34f3597450bf6a1f85f84897584", "git_parents": ["77ccd366e2143aad7346f25d1ebe76d5fa0dd13d"], "node": "3004e5aa583dd2daf86522da1ed3e17e1266a16a", "parents": ["e45adcf4a48b167dab5fdc4a0064fbfa2ca33f44"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666617, "git_changesets": ["f813d9152a23e34f3597450bf6a1f85f84897584"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1287": {"changesets": [{"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090592 - Adjust ImageDecoder cleanup during cycle collection.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341578\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342752\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/ImageDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "5680e97b06fdc00d4c75a9ba544d36e2b107ab94", "git_parents": ["f813d9152a23e34f3597450bf6a1f85f84897584"], "node": "dd0a84a89e4dcd043c514d97ae2b3eb1642fcda3", "parents": ["3004e5aa583dd2daf86522da1ed3e17e1266a16a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666660, "git_changesets": ["5680e97b06fdc00d4c75a9ba544d36e2b107ab94"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1288": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1986173: Restore history when typed value fixup fails  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341542\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342798\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_newtab_userTypedValue.js"], "git_node": "6fd325876a6015fc1436a402c4d4c182521119de", "git_parents": ["5680e97b06fdc00d4c75a9ba544d36e2b107ab94"], "node": "e65df9bdef08c27da31e476a7fc66af0555944fc", "parents": ["dd0a84a89e4dcd043c514d97ae2b3eb1642fcda3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794666694, "git_changesets": ["6fd325876a6015fc1436a402c4d4c182521119de"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1289": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079172, part 1 - Inline GraphWalker and ScanBlackVisitor into FloodBlackNode.  a=pascalc\n\nThey are only used in a single place, so inline it all to make it\neasier to understand.\n\nChange the aPi check in CheckedPush to be a release assert, for simplicity.\n\nWalkFromRoots is not used so it is removed.\n\nI marked FloodBlackNode MOZ_NEVER_INLINE to match GraphWalker::Walk,\nGraphWalker::DoWalk and ScanBlackVisitor::VisitNode.\n\nThis patch should not change the behavior.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338469\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342206\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.cpp"], "git_node": "71ce253b4ca6c8cbdbe0a03f4f6b2618c72de009", "git_parents": ["6fd325876a6015fc1436a402c4d4c182521119de"], "node": "73500c3f140031eec819f8d3a1c16c12e54f8817", "parents": ["e65df9bdef08c27da31e476a7fc66af0555944fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079172, part 2 - Use infallible allocation for Push in FloodBlackNode.  a=pascalc\n\nIf a cycle collection can't fully run due to running low on memory, it won't be\nable to free much of anything, so the memory problems will only get worse. If\nwe crash, then at least this issue will be visible in crash stats, as opposed\nto performance invisibly becoming terrible.\n\nThis requires removing a lot of failure propagation code.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338470\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342207\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.cpp"], "git_node": "d5ba01837d1b273dc2351d80604ed0d8316722d3", "git_parents": ["71ce253b4ca6c8cbdbe0a03f4f6b2618c72de009"], "node": "4122c81f3a39be411a885e44534d52f9b7812065", "parents": ["73500c3f140031eec819f8d3a1c16c12e54f8817"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079172, part 3 - Mark nodes black when they are pushed in FloodBlackNode.  a=pascalc\n\nPreviously, every child was pushed onto the queue, and filtered out when it was\npopped if it was already black or had not been traversed. This meant that the\nqueue could grow to the number of edges rather than the number of nodes. Doing\nthe check and marking the node black when it is pushed means each node is\npushed at most once. The resulting coloring and white node count are the same.\n\nRunning browser_aiwindow_smartbar_chat_active_navigate.js locally, this reduced\nthe maximum size of the queue from around 5600 nodes to 2800.\n\nThis probably makes locality worse, because we now look at a node when we push\nit, but I think that's a reasonable tradeoff for cutting memory usage in half.\n(Testing described in the last patch shows that the entire patch set improves\nScanBlockNodes performance over all.)\n\nThis is combined with the patches to make memory allocation infallible in the\nhope that it will reduce the rate of OOM crashes.\n\nRemove a WasTraversed check in ScanBlackNodes that is now redundant.\nThere's a check in PurpleScanBlackVisitor::Visit that is also redundant,\nbut that case is likely more common, so let's leave it to avoid the call\noverhead.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338471\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342208\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.cpp"], "git_node": "269f7c46544b7bd77c16749a9829d0dcee56877e", "git_parents": ["d5ba01837d1b273dc2351d80604ed0d8316722d3"], "node": "da54651b5d986d63a23917e65b7b7ead784aae8f", "parents": ["4122c81f3a39be411a885e44534d52f9b7812065"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079172, part 4 - Switch from nsDeque to Queue in FloodBlackNodes.  a=pascalc\n\nnsDeque uses a single block of memory, while Queue uses a segmented vector, so\nhopefully this will cause less OOMs. 1024 pointers seems big enough that\niterator overhead shouldn't be a big deal.\n\nWe already use infallible allocation with EdgeBlock, which each contain\n16 * 1024 pointers. Over the last week, those were about 7.6% of all\nOOM | small crashes.\n\nUnlike nsDeque, Queue has no inline storage, so creating one in each\nFloodBlackNode call would mean a heap allocation of a page for every call, which\ncan happen once per root. Instead, create the queue in ScanRoots and pass it\ndown. A drained Queue keeps its head page, so it is only allocated once. It\nwould be nice if it kept all of its empty pages but oh well.\n\nWhile running tests with big CCs, the full patch stack reduced the time spent\nin ScanBlackNodes() by 22% which sounds great but CC time is mostly dominated\nby building the graph so that's not much. The biggest improvement seen\nin a single CC was like 0.3ms.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338472\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342209\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.cpp"], "git_node": "f1eb6a62b87bb4014ac48ee83b62229bbafd3e27", "git_parents": ["269f7c46544b7bd77c16749a9829d0dcee56877e"], "node": "a949b25d7bfadf6cff4b877e691b2c37c564addd", "parents": ["da54651b5d986d63a23917e65b7b7ead784aae8f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794680616, "git_changesets": ["71ce253b4ca6c8cbdbe0a03f4f6b2618c72de009", "d5ba01837d1b273dc2351d80604ed0d8316722d3", "269f7c46544b7bd77c16749a9829d0dcee56877e", "f1eb6a62b87bb4014ac48ee83b62229bbafd3e27"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1290": {"changesets": [{"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089680.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342536\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342838\n", "files": ["image/VectorImage.cpp"], "git_node": "c2533346ba44f8dae47a07e676452fbe8a92a1b9", "git_parents": ["f1eb6a62b87bb4014ac48ee83b62229bbafd3e27"], "node": "a8ce91c10b5d909d2fa1cc51509d381215237407", "parents": ["a949b25d7bfadf6cff4b877e691b2c37c564addd"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794680641, "git_changesets": ["c2533346ba44f8dae47a07e676452fbe8a92a1b9"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1291": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088688 - Reuse UnscaledFont::CreateFromFontDescriptor for Moz2DImageRender.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339324\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339786\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/Moz2DImageRenderer.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/moz2d_renderer.rs"], "git_node": "05059960dfc80c4d5fa1bf62dc2e6e27ad6a54f9", "git_parents": ["c2533346ba44f8dae47a07e676452fbe8a92a1b9"], "node": "64f5035f21dd4bec0f263fa3d43725412d4d6eae", "parents": ["a8ce91c10b5d909d2fa1cc51509d381215237407"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088688 - Use ValidateFontDescriptor in WebRenderBridgeParent.  a=pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340641\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/ScaledFontFontconfig.cpp", "gfx/2d/UnscaledFontFreeType.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderTypes.h"], "git_node": "58a4458a136b9a2be23a60d5eafa4a79147e2583", "git_parents": ["05059960dfc80c4d5fa1bf62dc2e6e27ad6a54f9"], "node": "0385ab64c8704439837ac10ede901e8aac03fa27", "parents": ["64f5035f21dd4bec0f263fa3d43725412d4d6eae"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794749124, "git_changesets": ["05059960dfc80c4d5fa1bf62dc2e6e27ad6a54f9", "58a4458a136b9a2be23a60d5eafa4a79147e2583"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1292": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2024114 - Run valgrind tasks on the same worker type as builds.  a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nThis used to be the case until bug 1803831, where it was changed to some\nother worker type, and now the discrepancy with other builds is causing\nresource problems, where the t-linux-kvm pool is too short on memory.\n\nBack in bug 1803831, for some reason, the GCP workers had valgrind\ncrash, but that's not the case anymore, so we can just restore the old\nstatus quo.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310252\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342916\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/valgrind/kind.yml"], "git_node": "f9f6235f109f7ae0ec43e3304a844b9975fe83a0", "git_parents": ["58a4458a136b9a2be23a60d5eafa4a79147e2583"], "node": "befb4bc3a7cc8a5382c6ca0a9379e600e1af0857", "parents": ["0385ab64c8704439837ac10ede901e8aac03fa27"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794757497, "git_changesets": ["f9f6235f109f7ae0ec43e3304a844b9975fe83a0"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "1293": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\naf -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nan -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nar -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nast -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\naz -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nbe -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nbg -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nbn -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nbr -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nbs -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nca -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nca-valencia -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\ncak -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\ncs -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\ncy -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nda -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nde -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\ndsb -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nel -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nen-CA -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nen-GB -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\neo -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nes-AR -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nes-CL -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nes-ES -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nes-MX -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\net -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\neu -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nfa -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nff -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nfi -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nfr -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nfur -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbcb23a4c848c7\nfy-NL -\u003e 2727528d7a299d3d8f6d1b4f5cbbc